WEBVTT

00:01.480 --> 00:04.825
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.939 --> 00:08.242
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.293 --> 00:11.712
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.779 --> 00:14.665
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.749 --> 00:18.285
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.336 --> 00:21.472
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.539 --> 00:23.073
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.141 --> 00:24.525
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.592 --> 00:28.228
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.137 --> 00:37.838
Good evening, Quahog.
I'm Tom Tucker.

00:37.906 --> 00:39.073
Our top story tonight:

00:39.140 --> 00:40.607
In a shocking turn of events,

00:40.675 --> 00:43.010
the city of Detroit
has officially given up.

00:43.078 --> 00:45.679
The now former mayor has given
the key to the city

00:45.747 --> 00:47.314
back to the Huron Indian tribe.

00:47.382 --> 00:49.049
So, farewell, Detroit.

00:49.117 --> 00:52.820
From Bob Seger to Axel Foley,
we never really cared. Joyce?

00:52.887 --> 00:54.455
Thanks, Tom.
In local news,

00:54.522 --> 00:57.124
Quahog is expecting
a special guest this weekend,

00:57.192 --> 00:58.859
famed Asian
competitive eating champion

00:58.927 --> 01:00.861
Charles Yamamoto.

01:00.929 --> 01:03.397
Yamamoto has not yet lost
a hot dog eating competition

01:03.465 --> 01:04.765
on his world tour.

01:04.833 --> 01:06.934
But if you think
you have what it takes

01:07.001 --> 01:08.802
to beat the best eater
in the world,

01:08.870 --> 01:11.271
come down to the James Woods
High parking lot this Saturday

01:11.339 --> 01:13.307
with $50 and a large appetite.

01:13.374 --> 01:15.609
Wow, maybe you should
enter the contest, Dad.

01:15.677 --> 01:17.211
I'll bet
you could win.

01:17.278 --> 01:18.479
Well, I would, Chris,

01:18.546 --> 01:20.280
if I wasn't so
obsessed with my figure.

01:20.348 --> 01:21.598
Wait a minute.

01:21.666 --> 01:23.000
<i>Chris, have you ever
eaten anything?</i>

01:23.067 --> 01:24.685
Only, like, all the time!

01:24.752 --> 01:26.970
Perfect! Now we just
need the 50 bucks.

01:27.038 --> 01:29.623
Damn it, I knew I shouldn't
have named that star for Mort.

01:29.690 --> 01:32.309
Ugh! Just give me the money.

01:32.377 --> 01:33.560
Peter, we're not
spending $50

01:33.628 --> 01:35.512
so Chris can stuff his
face with hot dogs.

01:35.580 --> 01:36.814
All right, fine.

01:36.881 --> 01:39.032
I'll figure out a way
to get the cash myself.

01:39.100 --> 01:40.184
I'm a smart guy.

01:40.251 --> 01:41.752
Peter, no, you're not.

01:41.836 --> 01:44.655
Don't you feel ridiculous now?

01:47.926 --> 01:49.576
All right, Chris,
if we're gonna pay the entry fee

01:49.644 --> 01:50.811
for that eating contest,

01:50.878 --> 01:52.880
we got to sell some
of my old stuff.

01:52.947 --> 01:54.381
What are these, Dad?
Oh, wow.

01:54.432 --> 01:56.066
I haven't seen
those in a while.

01:56.151 --> 01:58.118
<i>Those are my old Playboys
from the '70s.</i>

01:58.186 --> 02:00.254
Oh, my God, this one's so hot.

02:00.321 --> 02:02.656
You can almost see
a little bit of woman.

02:02.724 --> 02:05.976
Wow, Peter, you've got some
pretty cool albums here.

02:06.044 --> 02:09.246
Yeah, well, I was one
cool potato back in the day.

02:09.330 --> 02:11.415
You know, some of these might
actually be worth something.

02:11.482 --> 02:13.400
Look at this--
Beatles, Rolling Stones.

02:13.451 --> 02:15.886
Oh, my God, I haven't seen
this one in forever.

02:15.954 --> 02:17.838
<i>Look-Look at this. Queen,
News of the World.</i>

02:17.905 --> 02:20.140
Check it out.

02:20.208 --> 02:21.275
Aah!

02:21.342 --> 02:22.543
Oh, what's the matter?

02:22.610 --> 02:24.711
What the hell is that?!
A killer robot monster?!

02:24.779 --> 02:26.146
<i>No, it's News of the World.</i>

02:26.214 --> 02:27.747
It's an album
by the band Queen. See?

02:27.799 --> 02:29.433
Aah!
Stewie, relax.

02:29.517 --> 02:31.752
No, Brian! You keep
that thing away from me!

02:31.819 --> 02:33.921
Is it... Is it looking at me?!

02:33.988 --> 02:35.756
Can it see me?!

02:35.823 --> 02:37.758
(laughing): Man, you're really scared
of this thing, huh?

02:37.825 --> 02:39.193
Does it eat little boys?!

02:39.260 --> 02:41.361
I don't know. Maybe,
if it's hungry.

02:41.429 --> 02:43.730
(yelling)

02:45.817 --> 02:48.235
Here's 50 bucks.
I'm taking this album.

02:48.286 --> 02:49.753
Oh, wow, check
it out, Chris!

02:49.821 --> 02:51.889
We got our entry fee
for the eating contest!

02:51.956 --> 02:53.407
Now for the
next five days,

02:53.474 --> 02:55.025
we're gonna focus on
nothing but training.

02:55.093 --> 02:56.927
We'll even get up at
the crack of dawn.

02:59.097 --> 03:00.631
(snoring)

03:00.698 --> 03:02.733
(whispering):
Dad?

03:02.800 --> 03:05.269
Dad, it's time to get up.

03:05.336 --> 03:08.722
Oh, jeez, Chris,
it's the crack of dawn.

03:08.790 --> 03:11.058
Yeah, but Dad, you
said to wake you up.

03:11.125 --> 03:12.759
Yeah... Yeah, but, uh...

03:12.827 --> 03:14.027
(mumbling)

03:14.095 --> 03:15.345
Just... get-get...
get in...

03:15.430 --> 03:17.614
get in the bed
with me and your mom.

03:17.682 --> 03:19.416
Okay, but what
about training?

03:19.484 --> 03:21.551
Oh, you smell
like melted cheese.

03:21.619 --> 03:24.721
Yummy, yummy, yummy,
yummy, yummy, yummy, yummy.

03:29.427 --> 03:31.895
(yawns) Good morning, Rupert.

03:31.963 --> 03:35.265
Please tell me you set the timer
on the coffeemaker

03:35.333 --> 03:37.084
because I completely forgot.

03:37.151 --> 03:38.335
(yelling)

03:38.419 --> 03:39.870
(laughing)

03:39.954 --> 03:41.371
You son of a bitch!

03:41.456 --> 03:43.924
Good morning.
Thought I'd help you wake up.

03:43.992 --> 03:45.993
God, why does he look sad?!

03:46.060 --> 03:47.427
He's already
destroyed mankind!

03:47.495 --> 03:49.062
What else could he want?!

03:51.099 --> 03:52.416
Hey, Carl.

03:52.483 --> 03:54.768
Hey, can I get a couple
of scratch-off lottery tickets?

03:54.836 --> 03:56.353
Oh, sure, Brian.

03:56.437 --> 03:58.772
Ooh, Brian, can I do one?
I love scratchers!

03:58.840 --> 04:00.257
Well, all right,
maybe just one.

04:01.509 --> 04:03.193
Cherry.

04:03.278 --> 04:04.378
Another cherry.

04:04.445 --> 04:06.730
Oh, come on, one more, one more!

04:07.932 --> 04:09.833
(yelling)

04:09.901 --> 04:11.151
Thanks, Carl.

04:11.219 --> 04:12.486
Yeah, you're welcome.
That was fun.

04:12.553 --> 04:14.154
See you later.

04:14.222 --> 04:15.395
Hey, uh, thanks
for letting me be Yoda.

04:15.420 --> 04:16.620
Yup.

04:22.347 --> 04:23.914
What is this?

04:30.688 --> 04:34.224
("Pop Goes the Weasel" plays)

04:34.292 --> 04:34.958
(music stops)

04:35.026 --> 04:35.892
(music stops)

04:35.960 --> 04:37.194
(music resumes)

04:39.163 --> 04:41.398
(music stops)

04:41.466 --> 04:43.166
(music resumes)

04:45.136 --> 04:46.136
(music stops)

04:48.239 --> 04:49.489
(boing)

04:49.557 --> 04:52.242
Oh-ho-ho,
what was I worried about?

04:52.310 --> 04:54.060
Aah! Aah! Aah!
Oh, God!

04:54.112 --> 04:55.479
Aah! Aah!

04:55.546 --> 04:57.014
He's bleeding, man!

04:57.081 --> 04:59.566
He's bleeding, and nobody's
doing anything about it!

04:59.634 --> 05:01.802
I'll tell you what the news
of the world is.

05:01.869 --> 05:03.470
We're in a lot
of (bleep) trouble!

05:03.538 --> 05:05.405
(cheering and applause)

05:07.642 --> 05:09.009
All right, Chris,
this is it.

05:09.077 --> 05:10.644
This is what we've
been working for.

05:10.712 --> 05:12.713
If you get nervous, just
picture the audience naked

05:12.780 --> 05:14.514
and slide those hot
dogs down your throat.

05:14.582 --> 05:16.283
Ladies and gentlemen, welcome

05:16.351 --> 05:19.820
to the World Hot Dog Eating
Championship Competition!

05:19.887 --> 05:22.422
Please welcome our undefeated
champion eater,

05:22.490 --> 05:24.791
Charles Yamamoto!

05:24.859 --> 05:26.710
(cheering and applause)

05:29.313 --> 05:31.732
Oh, my God, that guy is huge.

05:32.934 --> 05:35.118
All right, eaters,
you have ten minutes.

05:35.186 --> 05:38.038
On your marks,
get set, eat!

05:48.433 --> 05:51.418
(cheering and whistling)

05:57.625 --> 05:59.009
Come on, Chris.
You're doing great.

05:59.093 --> 06:00.777
Just keep going.
You're almost there.

06:00.845 --> 06:02.796
Well, I'd better get a move on.

06:08.603 --> 06:09.903
Time's almost up!

06:09.971 --> 06:11.471
It's gonna be a close one!

06:14.692 --> 06:15.909
Chris, you're four
hot dogs behind!

06:15.976 --> 06:17.077
Come on! Hurry!

06:17.144 --> 06:20.280
Oh! I can't eat anymore.

06:20.348 --> 06:22.249
Remember what I told you.

06:22.316 --> 06:25.952
I get these weird cyst things
right on the fringe of my sac.

06:26.020 --> 06:27.621
I want to get 'em checked,

06:27.688 --> 06:29.656
but I'm afraid
of what they're gonna tell me.

06:29.724 --> 06:31.658
<i>He's right. I can do it!</i>

06:39.183 --> 06:40.317
(buzzer sounds, cheering)

06:40.384 --> 06:41.785
ANNOUNCER:
We have a winner!

06:41.853 --> 06:45.639
Ladies and gentlemen, Yamamoto
has finally been defeated!

06:45.690 --> 06:48.058
(cheering, applause
and whistling)

06:48.126 --> 06:50.243
Chris, you did it.
You're a champion!

06:50.311 --> 06:52.245
And now you get your
pick of the groupies.

06:54.248 --> 06:55.549
They're shiny.

06:55.616 --> 06:56.983
Yeah, it's a
pretty warm day.

07:00.922 --> 07:02.539
Oh!

07:02.623 --> 07:03.824
Hey, hey, hey,
there, champ!

07:03.891 --> 07:05.225
Aw, look at
him, Lois.

07:05.293 --> 07:06.593
Relaxing after
his big victory.

07:06.661 --> 07:08.195
Peter, he's not relaxing.

07:08.262 --> 07:10.063
He's in a great deal of pain.

07:10.131 --> 07:12.466
Damn it, don't you
see what you did to him?

07:12.533 --> 07:15.068
I told you not to take him
to that eating competition,

07:15.136 --> 07:16.586
and you deliberately defied me!

07:16.654 --> 07:18.355
All right, what's
this really about?

07:18.422 --> 07:20.490
Peter, Chris is
already overweight.

07:20.558 --> 07:23.527
We need to start taking
responsibility for his health.

07:23.594 --> 07:25.962
So I decided to sign him up
for fat camp.

07:26.030 --> 07:28.899
What?! Mom, I don't want
to go to fat camp!

07:28.966 --> 07:31.334
I'm sorry, sweetie.
It's for your own good.

07:31.402 --> 07:34.304
And trust me, you'll feel
much better about yourself.

07:34.372 --> 07:36.890
Everyone's gonna
make fun of me!

07:36.958 --> 07:39.192
Oh, come on, who's
gonna make fun of you?

07:39.243 --> 07:41.278
Hey, fatty, I hear
you're going to fat camp.

07:41.345 --> 07:42.379
That's where
you belong!

07:42.446 --> 07:43.980
Peter, stop it!

07:44.048 --> 07:46.283
And I'd better not see
you at the big dance!

07:46.367 --> 07:47.584
Come on, you.

07:47.652 --> 07:49.886
Sorry, Chris.
I-I'm gonna go with him.

08:11.415 --> 08:13.532
Hi. Welcome to
Camp Fresh Start.

08:13.600 --> 08:15.534
Yeah, our son's gross,
so here we are.

08:15.602 --> 08:16.852
The name's
Griffin.

08:16.920 --> 08:18.087
Ah, yes,
Chris Griffin.

08:18.154 --> 08:20.273
We have you staying
in the Broccoli Cabin.

08:20.340 --> 08:22.441
So you guys are just
gonna leave me here?

08:22.509 --> 08:24.343
Yeah, honey.
That's what camp is.

08:24.411 --> 08:25.845
I don't want to stay!

08:25.913 --> 08:27.663
Please take me home!

08:27.731 --> 08:30.032
I don't want to go to fat camp!

08:30.100 --> 08:31.734
Aw, come on, Chris.
Your mother's right.

08:31.802 --> 08:33.169
This'll be good for you.

08:33.237 --> 08:35.037
Well, how come you
don't have to go?!

08:35.105 --> 08:36.539
You're fatter
than I am!

08:36.607 --> 08:38.040
Huh. Good question, Peter.

08:38.108 --> 08:39.842
<i>How come
you don't have to go?</i>

08:39.910 --> 08:41.043
What are you
talking about?

08:41.111 --> 08:42.678
Well, you're the one
who entered him

08:42.746 --> 08:44.080
in that hot dog
eating contest.

08:44.147 --> 08:45.448
Besides, he's right.

08:45.515 --> 08:47.617
<i>You could stand to lose
a few pounds yourself.</i>

08:47.684 --> 08:49.552
Unless you don't think
you could handle it.

08:49.620 --> 08:51.354
Oh, yeah?

08:51.421 --> 08:52.521
Well, I think I can.

08:52.589 --> 08:53.789
What was that?

08:53.857 --> 08:55.391
Never you mind
what that was.

08:55.459 --> 08:57.526
(birds singing)

08:57.594 --> 08:58.995
(trash can lid clanging)

08:59.062 --> 09:00.546
Rise and shine, everyone!

09:01.715 --> 09:02.915
What do you got there?

09:03.000 --> 09:04.267
A candy bar, huh?

09:04.334 --> 09:05.568
Got any other
contraband?

09:05.636 --> 09:06.869
No.
Don't lie to me.

09:06.937 --> 09:08.437
My father was a lawyer.

09:08.505 --> 09:09.972
Oh, so your dad
gets guys off.

09:10.040 --> 09:11.240
(laughing)

09:11.308 --> 09:12.341
Peter Griffin.
Cabin clown.

09:12.392 --> 09:14.010
Where's your bag, fatty?

09:14.077 --> 09:16.012
You're welcome to
search my "beef case."

09:16.079 --> 09:18.064
But there's
"mutton" in there.

09:18.131 --> 09:19.715
(laughs) Peter Griffin.
Cabin clown.

09:19.783 --> 09:21.584
You're in big trouble, mister.

09:21.652 --> 09:24.353
Oh, there's no pulling the
wool over this guy's eyes.

09:24.421 --> 09:26.572
Looks like I'd better
go on the "lamb."

09:26.640 --> 09:28.424
Peter Griffin.
Cabin clown.

09:31.411 --> 09:34.196
I think I'm gonna do okay here
at fat camp.

09:34.264 --> 09:36.399
You sure you got
the "chops" for it?

09:36.466 --> 09:38.150
Knock it off.
I'm the cabin clown.

09:38.218 --> 09:40.069
(owl hooting)

09:43.907 --> 09:45.841
And then he went
into the kitchen,

09:45.909 --> 09:49.595
slowly opened the refrigerator,
and it was empty!

09:49.663 --> 09:50.513
(all gasp)

09:50.580 --> 09:51.914
So then, the man,

09:51.965 --> 09:53.849
weak with hunger,
raced from the refrigerator

09:53.917 --> 09:56.519
to the counter
to look for a delivery menu,

09:56.586 --> 09:59.422
but all he could find was one
for a vegan place!

09:59.489 --> 10:01.240
(all yell)

10:01.308 --> 10:03.025
Vegan places aren't
real, right?

10:03.093 --> 10:06.028
No, they're not real.
Or are they?!

10:06.096 --> 10:07.196
Aah! Salad!

10:07.263 --> 10:09.432
(all yelling)

10:09.499 --> 10:10.933
Thank you
for sharing, Leonard.

10:11.001 --> 10:13.435
<i>And I think getting a new couch
was the way to go.</i>

10:13.487 --> 10:15.304
Is there someone else
who has a story

10:15.372 --> 10:16.572
they'd like to share? Peter?

10:16.640 --> 10:17.840
Uh, yeah, sure.

10:17.908 --> 10:19.909
This one time,
I was on a city bus,

10:19.976 --> 10:21.444
and the guy next to me

10:21.511 --> 10:23.245
was eating a bucket
of fried chicken.

10:23.313 --> 10:24.980
- Mmm! - Ooh!
Yum!

10:25.048 --> 10:27.316
And the smell was
getting to me, you know.

10:27.384 --> 10:29.518
And even though
I didn't know the guy,

10:29.586 --> 10:31.220
I just dug in

10:31.288 --> 10:33.289
and started stuffing
that chicken into my mouth.

10:33.357 --> 10:34.423
O-Oh!
Embarrassing.

10:34.491 --> 10:35.691
I've done that.

10:35.759 --> 10:37.093
It was so delicious.

10:37.160 --> 10:39.729
But... it wasn't
fried chicken.

10:39.796 --> 10:41.964
It was a baby!

10:42.032 --> 10:44.700
(crying):
It was a baby.

10:44.768 --> 10:46.218
(sobbing)

10:50.807 --> 10:51.941
Stewie?

10:52.008 --> 10:54.810
Rupert, we won't give
that evil robot

10:54.878 --> 10:56.445
the satisfaction of killing us.

10:56.513 --> 10:59.198
We'll go together
on our own terms.

10:59.266 --> 11:01.283
See you on the other side.

11:01.334 --> 11:02.284
(gunshot)

11:02.352 --> 11:03.252
Oh, my God!

11:03.320 --> 11:04.670
Stewie, no!

11:04.738 --> 11:06.072
What the hell's
wrong with you?!

11:06.139 --> 11:07.506
It's that robot!

11:07.574 --> 11:09.775
He killed Queen,
and now he's going to kill me!

11:09.843 --> 11:11.077
He didn't kill Queen.

11:11.144 --> 11:12.211
They're all fine.

11:12.279 --> 11:14.063
Most of them are fine.

11:14.131 --> 11:16.082
Look, Stewie, I'm sorry
for scaring you, all right?

11:16.149 --> 11:18.217
But come on,
it's not a real robot.

11:18.301 --> 11:20.335
See? It, It's
just an album. Look.

11:20.387 --> 11:22.288
Here, you want
to hit it?

11:22.355 --> 11:24.957
Well... I'm usually more
comfortable around things

11:25.025 --> 11:26.992
if I can put them
in my mouth.

11:27.060 --> 11:28.844
So, can I put it
in my mouth?

11:28.895 --> 11:29.962
I guess.

11:31.531 --> 11:33.032
This is just an album!

11:33.100 --> 11:35.551
Yeah, that's what I've
been trying to tell you.

11:35.619 --> 11:37.420
So, you know,
can you forgive me?

11:37.487 --> 11:39.872
Oh, I suppose so.

11:39.940 --> 11:41.807
I mean, Magellan forgave
the "Land Ho" prankster.

11:41.875 --> 11:43.109
Land ho!

11:43.176 --> 11:44.360
Where?! Where?!

11:44.428 --> 11:45.761
Psych! Made you
look, loser.

11:45.829 --> 11:47.096
Good thing
there wasn't land

11:47.164 --> 11:49.064
or else you'd have
to meet the natives

11:49.132 --> 11:50.766
with that mustard stain on your shirt.
What stain?

11:50.834 --> 11:51.967
Ah! (blows raspberry)

11:52.035 --> 11:54.336
Ugh! Why did I even bring
you on this trip?!

11:54.404 --> 11:55.738
Because I'm the best
damn land spotter

11:55.806 --> 11:56.939
in all of Europe.

11:57.007 --> 11:58.474
It's true.
You are the best.

11:58.542 --> 12:00.443
Yeah, I don't need you
to tell me that.

12:00.510 --> 12:02.478
(birds chirping)

12:02.546 --> 12:04.346
(both panting)

12:04.414 --> 12:06.348
Dad, I can't take
this anymore.

12:06.416 --> 12:10.386
I'm so tired
and I'm so hungry.

12:10.454 --> 12:12.238
I got an idea, Chris.
Follow me.

12:13.740 --> 12:14.890
What are we doing?

12:14.941 --> 12:17.359
I saw a forest like this
in a book one time,

12:17.410 --> 12:19.628
and I know there's a gingerbread
house out here somewhere.

12:19.696 --> 12:21.030
Do you think
we could find it?!

12:21.097 --> 12:22.982
We have to, Chris.
We-we gotta eat something

12:23.049 --> 12:24.283
besides what
they're feeding us.

12:24.351 --> 12:26.018
I know what
you mean, Dad.

12:26.086 --> 12:28.687
I'm so hungry I could
eat this dead camper.

12:28.755 --> 12:29.989
Holy crap!

12:30.056 --> 12:31.991
(flies buzzing)

12:35.896 --> 12:38.464
Well, we clearly don't have
all the evidence yet,

12:38.532 --> 12:40.599
but that's never
stopped us before, right?

12:40.667 --> 12:41.901
(laughs)

12:44.154 --> 12:46.021
Oh, there's no other cops here.

12:46.089 --> 12:49.024
But we do know one thing,
this kid was murdered.

12:49.092 --> 12:50.192
(all gasp)

12:50.260 --> 12:51.527
Murdered?!
Who in the world

12:51.595 --> 12:52.761
would want to
kill a camper?

12:52.829 --> 12:54.363
Don't look at me.

12:54.431 --> 12:55.948
I'm just here to
drop off my son.

12:56.032 --> 13:00.452
Justin? Justin,
that does not work for me.

13:00.520 --> 13:02.288
And it looks like there
are signs of trauma

13:02.355 --> 13:03.789
around the throat.

13:03.857 --> 13:05.758
Somebody strangled
this fat kid.

13:05.825 --> 13:07.159
Wait. He was strangled?

13:07.227 --> 13:08.227
Yeah.

13:08.295 --> 13:09.628
Joe, I know
who did it.

13:09.696 --> 13:11.163
You do? Who?

13:11.231 --> 13:12.915
Well, there's
only one person I know

13:12.966 --> 13:14.633
who likes to strangle fat guys:

13:14.718 --> 13:16.452
Patrick Pewterschmidt.

13:16.520 --> 13:17.253
Who's that?

13:17.320 --> 13:19.555
My brother-in-law.

13:19.622 --> 13:22.808
<i>People call him
"The Fat Guy Strangler."</i>

13:22.893 --> 13:26.295
<i>He's always had a thing
for strangling fat guys.</i>

13:26.346 --> 13:28.831
I guess he fits
the profile, Peter,

13:28.899 --> 13:31.100
but Lois's brother is
locked up in an asylum.

13:31.167 --> 13:33.302
Well, either way,
we gotta get out of here.

13:33.370 --> 13:34.737
Otherwise,
we're just sitting ducks!

13:34.804 --> 13:37.573
Hey, we all know this guy
goes for the classy ladies.

13:37.641 --> 13:39.174
In fact, I once
caught him trying

13:39.242 --> 13:40.442
to pick up
a quack whore.

13:40.510 --> 13:42.695
(all laugh)

13:42.779 --> 13:44.013
All right, calm down.

13:44.080 --> 13:46.015
We all make bad choices.

13:48.118 --> 13:49.218
(phone rings)

13:49.286 --> 13:50.252
Hello?

13:50.320 --> 13:51.554
Lois, I hope
you're sitting down.

13:51.621 --> 13:52.755
I got something
to tell ya.

13:52.822 --> 13:54.156
Oh, God, what's wrong?

13:54.224 --> 13:56.075
Is everything okay?
Is it Chris?

13:56.142 --> 13:57.543
No, it's Peter,
your husband.

13:57.611 --> 13:59.178
But I'm calling
with big news.

13:59.246 --> 14:00.879
I was Anita in
the camp production

14:00.947 --> 14:02.314
<i>of West Side Story.</i>

14:02.382 --> 14:04.783
Peter, you know you're terrible
at patter songs.

14:04.851 --> 14:06.452
I did okay.

14:06.519 --> 14:08.837
♪ (mumbles lyrics) ...America ♪

14:08.888 --> 14:10.472
♪ (mumbles) ...America ♪

14:10.540 --> 14:11.673
♪ (mumbling) ...America ♪

14:11.725 --> 14:15.094
♪ (mumbling) ...America. ♪

14:15.161 --> 14:16.395
I got other news, too.

14:16.463 --> 14:18.631
One of the fat kids at camp
got strangled!

14:18.698 --> 14:20.266
(gasps) Oh, my God!

14:20.333 --> 14:22.134
Yeah, but don't worry.
It ain't your brother.

14:22.202 --> 14:23.569
He's still locked up
in that asylum.

14:23.637 --> 14:26.005
Um, Mom...

14:26.072 --> 14:27.840
look who dropped
by for a visit.

14:29.209 --> 14:31.110
Hello, Lois.

14:31.177 --> 14:32.511
(gasps) Patrick!

14:32.579 --> 14:33.779
It's been
a long time.

14:33.847 --> 14:36.131
(hushed):
Peter, he's here!

14:36.199 --> 14:38.133
Wait a second, Lois,
I want to go back

14:38.201 --> 14:40.002
to what you said
about my patter singing.

14:40.070 --> 14:41.303
Who gives you
the right?!

14:41.371 --> 14:42.705
<i>You know I carried
Pirates of Penzance</i>

14:42.772 --> 14:45.274
that season at Quahog
Community Theater.

14:45.342 --> 14:48.510
♪ I am the
(sings gibberish) ...general ♪

14:48.578 --> 14:51.013
♪ (sings gibberish) ...mineral ♪

14:51.081 --> 14:53.449
♪ (sings gibberish)
...historical ♪

14:53.516 --> 14:55.517
♪ (sings gibberish)
...with the eggs on top. ♪

15:01.701 --> 15:03.651
Man, I hope we get back
to your house

15:03.703 --> 15:05.620
before Patrick hurts
anyone else!

15:05.671 --> 15:07.706
If he even lays
a finger on my family,

15:07.790 --> 15:09.874
I'll do to him
what I did to the Riddler.

15:20.136 --> 15:21.386
(tires squeal)

15:21.470 --> 15:23.071
Freeze, psycho!

15:23.139 --> 15:24.606
Oh, Peter, thank God!

15:24.674 --> 15:26.441
Patrick Pewterschmidt,
you're under arrest

15:26.509 --> 15:29.444
for the murder of, uh...
(bleep)

15:29.512 --> 15:31.546
I didn't get
the kid's name.

15:31.614 --> 15:33.048
We're supposed to do that.

15:33.115 --> 15:34.566
Lois, you called
the cops?

15:34.633 --> 15:38.370
Patrick, you're my brother and
I love you, but you're not well.

15:38.437 --> 15:39.621
But I'm better now.

15:39.688 --> 15:40.889
I've put my past
behind me.

15:40.956 --> 15:42.223
Save it, Patrick.

15:42.291 --> 15:45.026
We know you escaped
from the asylum and killed...

15:45.094 --> 15:46.895
Bill, we'll just call him
"Bill" for now.

15:46.962 --> 15:48.563
Escaped?
I-I didn't escape.

15:48.631 --> 15:51.199
Just this morning, a very nice
gentleman opened my cell door

15:51.267 --> 15:52.967
and said I was
free to go.

15:53.035 --> 15:55.337
Yeah, nice try.
That's not how it works.

15:55.404 --> 15:58.440
Uncle Patrick, why do you
strangle fat people?

15:58.507 --> 15:59.808
It's probably
a weird fetish thing.

15:59.875 --> 16:01.376
Some criminals have 'em.

16:01.444 --> 16:03.111
Like those anal-retentive
bandits

16:03.179 --> 16:04.779
who robbed Quahog Bank
last year.

16:04.847 --> 16:07.282
All right, hands in the air!
Vertically!

16:07.350 --> 16:09.184
Both arms should be
parallel to each other!

16:09.235 --> 16:11.736
You, fill this bag with clean,
unmarked bills!

16:11.821 --> 16:14.723
But first fix that notepad
so it's at a right angle

16:14.790 --> 16:16.191
with the corner of your desk!

16:16.258 --> 16:18.410
And tap that pile of receipts
against a flat surface

16:18.494 --> 16:19.861
so they're not sticking out
haphazardly!

16:19.929 --> 16:21.229
You know what?!
Forget about the money!

16:21.280 --> 16:22.364
Everybody grab a broom!

16:22.431 --> 16:23.565
We are straightening
this place up!

16:27.053 --> 16:28.219
All right, campers,

16:28.287 --> 16:29.888
until the Fat Guy Strangler
is caught,

16:29.955 --> 16:32.290
everyone has to stay
inside their cabins.

16:32.358 --> 16:33.892
Now I'm gonna do
a stomach count.

16:33.959 --> 16:35.660
When I call your name,
please respond.

16:35.728 --> 16:36.694
Jenkins?

16:36.762 --> 16:37.662
(stomach growls)

16:37.730 --> 16:38.696
Robertson?

16:38.764 --> 16:39.664
(stomach growls)

16:39.732 --> 16:40.732
Davis?

16:40.800 --> 16:42.567
(stomach growls)
Elliot?

16:42.635 --> 16:43.468
Where's Elliot?

16:43.536 --> 16:44.936
I think he's asleep.

16:45.004 --> 16:47.472
Elliot?
Elliot, wake up.

16:47.540 --> 16:49.958
Elliot? (gasps)

16:50.025 --> 16:51.459
(phone rings)

16:51.527 --> 16:52.861
Officer Swanson here.

16:52.928 --> 16:54.763
What?! Oh, my God!

16:54.830 --> 16:56.498
What is it, Joe?

16:56.565 --> 16:58.600
Another camper was strangled
half an hour ago.

16:58.667 --> 17:00.869
But... that means...

17:00.936 --> 17:03.037
Patrick can't be
the killer.

17:03.105 --> 17:05.006
That's what I was
trying to tell you.

17:05.074 --> 17:06.641
Acknowledged. I'm on it.

17:06.709 --> 17:08.410
Joe, would you settle
a camp argument?

17:08.477 --> 17:10.378
Is it "Bombardment"
or "Dodgeball"?

17:10.446 --> 17:11.146
Dodgeball.

17:11.213 --> 17:12.247
Ah, you don't know.

17:12.314 --> 17:13.948
Well, I'd better
put out an APB

17:14.016 --> 17:15.483
to all
the neighboring towns.

17:15.551 --> 17:17.352
Oh, the murderer won't leave
the camp.

17:17.420 --> 17:19.320
What?
What are you talking about?

17:19.388 --> 17:20.755
He's "feeding."

17:20.806 --> 17:22.891
He killed twice and
he's gonna do it again.

17:22.958 --> 17:25.510
He's got plenty of places
to hide out there

17:25.594 --> 17:27.061
and a fully stocked corral
of victims.

17:27.129 --> 17:28.513
How do you know that?

17:28.581 --> 17:30.398
Trust me. I know.

17:30.466 --> 17:32.584
You know, Joe, maybe Patrick can
actually be of help.

17:32.651 --> 17:35.036
I mean, who better to get
inside the mind of someone

17:35.104 --> 17:37.372
who's strangling fat people
than someone who's done it himself?

17:37.440 --> 17:38.706
Yeah, give him a chance, Joe.

17:38.774 --> 17:40.542
Like I did with scary teenagers.

17:40.609 --> 17:42.877
I used to be afraid of 'em,
until I realized

17:42.945 --> 17:44.212
they were just misunderstood.

17:44.280 --> 17:46.114
Hey, fat ass,
give me your wallet!

17:46.182 --> 17:47.415
<i>I could give you
my wallet,</i>

17:47.483 --> 17:49.851
but what I think
you really want...

17:49.919 --> 17:51.186
is love.

17:51.253 --> 17:52.854
(voice breaks):
It's true!

17:58.244 --> 17:59.477
I'm taking your shoes.

18:06.318 --> 18:07.535
Poor kid.

18:07.603 --> 18:08.937
You know,
the weirdest thing is

18:09.004 --> 18:10.555
his bunk is right next
to Chris's.

18:10.623 --> 18:11.956
Yeah, that was
a close call.

18:12.024 --> 18:13.992
Oh, it was more
than a close call.

18:14.059 --> 18:16.661
You said the first victim was
wearing a baseball cap,

18:16.729 --> 18:18.196
this second one is blond...

18:18.264 --> 18:20.398
<i>The killer wasn't trying
to murder this kid.</i>

18:20.483 --> 18:22.400
He was trying to murder Chris.

18:22.468 --> 18:23.935
(gasps) Oh, my God!

18:24.003 --> 18:26.187
W-Why would anyone
want to kill Chris?

18:26.255 --> 18:27.639
I don't know,
but I do know

18:27.706 --> 18:29.841
that he's in a great deal
of danger right now.

18:29.909 --> 18:31.392
Come on. Let's go!
Yeah!

18:31.460 --> 18:34.229
But wait, this is our last
chance to do a panty raid!

18:34.296 --> 18:35.547
(women scream)

18:35.631 --> 18:37.248
Yay! Fat camp!
We got it!

18:37.333 --> 18:39.200
Oh, no, a gust of wind!

18:45.691 --> 18:47.525
(rustling)

18:52.181 --> 18:54.482
(creaking)

18:55.935 --> 18:58.686
(gasps) Wha, what
are you doing here?

18:58.754 --> 19:00.588
You dishonored me,
Chris Griffin.

19:00.656 --> 19:03.241
No one has ever eaten
more hot dogs than me.

19:03.309 --> 19:05.059
Now you must die!

19:07.613 --> 19:09.948
(gagging)
(glass shattering)

19:14.086 --> 19:15.253
(groans)

19:16.171 --> 19:17.238
(gasps)

19:22.111 --> 19:24.045
(gagging)

19:33.439 --> 19:34.755
STEWIE: Hey, fat ass!

19:36.225 --> 19:37.825
I got news for you.

19:37.893 --> 19:40.995
<i>The News of the World!</i>

19:41.063 --> 19:42.230
(screams)

19:42.298 --> 19:44.232
Why does robot hold
dead people?!

19:44.300 --> 19:45.950
Is that future or past?!

19:46.035 --> 19:47.902
(gasping and groaning)

19:51.590 --> 19:54.876
Oh, my God, Stewie,
you saved my life!

19:54.943 --> 19:56.861
Ah, you would've done
the same for me, Chris.

19:56.929 --> 19:59.197
The important thing is,
we're all gonna be okay.

19:59.265 --> 20:00.548
Right, Giant Robot?

20:10.859 --> 20:14.862
Charles Yamamoto...
went from eating champion

20:14.930 --> 20:16.264
to cold-blooded killer.

20:16.332 --> 20:17.498
Who'd have thought?

20:17.566 --> 20:19.400
Wait a minute, Joe.
That's the guy who opened

20:19.468 --> 20:21.302
the door to my cell
yesterday and told me

20:21.370 --> 20:22.437
I could leave
the asylum.

20:22.504 --> 20:24.105
Huh. Is that right?

20:24.173 --> 20:25.673
Well, then it
all makes sense.

20:25.741 --> 20:26.941
Yamamoto wanted it
to look like

20:27.009 --> 20:28.910
you broke out
on your own.

20:28.978 --> 20:30.345
That way,
when he murdered Chris,

20:30.412 --> 20:33.114
it was a cinch that you would
take the blame.

20:33.182 --> 20:37.051
Well, Patrick, I guess
we all owe you an apology.

20:37.119 --> 20:38.086
Patrick?

20:38.153 --> 20:40.021
Where did he go?

20:40.089 --> 20:41.389
He was just
right here.

20:41.457 --> 20:42.423
What happened?!

20:44.076 --> 20:45.660
Damn it!
He must've gotten away!

20:45.728 --> 20:46.928
How is that possible?!

20:46.996 --> 20:48.796
I don't know,
but I'd better make it

20:48.864 --> 20:50.398
look like there
was a struggle.

20:50.466 --> 20:51.666
Someone punch me
in the face.

20:52.918 --> 20:54.452
I'm a good friend
to you.

20:54.453 --> 21:55.453
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru